{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You came in with nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea again—can you tell me how you’ve been feeling since you got home from the hospital three days ago?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not better, honestly. The nausea never went away. I tried to eat a little, but I just couldn’t keep anything down. The diarrhea’s still there too—watery, no blood. I was so weak I had to come back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And any fever, chills, or new abdominal pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever. Just the same dull pain I’ve had for years around my stomach and near the G-tube. Nothing worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Your labs show your potassium is normal, but your AST and alkaline phosphatase are a bit high—probably from dehydration or your liver history. No signs of infection in your blood so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it still the norovirus? I thought that was supposed to go away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely. Sometimes it lasts longer in people with gastric surgery. We’re not repeating stool tests since you just had them. We’ll treat it as ongoing viral gastroenteritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. So what’s the plan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you IV fluids to rehydrate you, and we’ll keep giving you Zofran for nausea. We’ll start you on clear liquids tomorrow and see how you do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I use my G-tube for feeds? That’s how I got nutrition before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re holding off on tube feeds for now. They might make the diarrhea worse while your gut is still inflamed. We’ll rely on your mouth for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. What about my iron pill? I usually take it every day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re holding your iron for now—it can worsen nausea. You’ll restart it at home when you’re feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my pain meds? I’ve been using the liquid oxycodone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re using acetaminophen and gabapentin for now. We’re limiting opioids because they can slow the gut and make nausea worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I understand. I just don’t want the pain to flare up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-10-26 18:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor closely. If it gets bad, we’ll adjust. For now, rest and let your gut heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-10-27 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs this morning show your white count is a bit low, but stable. Potassium dropped a little—3.7—so we’ll watch that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-10-27 07:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous? The low white count?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-10-27 07:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. It can happen with viral infections. We’re not seeing signs of bacterial infection, so we’re not worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-10-27 07:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, good. I was able to sip some broth last night without throwing up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-10-27 07:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. We’ll advance you to clear liquids today—apple juice, broth, maybe some Jell-O. Small sips."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-10-27 07:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I try a soft food later, like mashed potatoes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-10-27 07:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Let’s see how you do today. If no nausea or vomiting, we can try soft foods tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-10-27 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s your stomach doing? Any nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-10-27 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little queasy, but not bad. I had half a cup of apple juice an hour ago and it stayed down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-10-27 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. I’ll order another dose of Zofran to keep that nausea in check."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-10-27 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m really hoping I can eat more soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-10-27 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on the right track. Your body just needs time to recover from the virus."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-10-28 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your labs are looking better. White count is up, potassium is 3.8—still a bit low but improving. You made it through the night without vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-10-28 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes! I had broth and crackers for dinner and a protein shake before bed. All stayed down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-10-28 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s fantastic. We’ll advance you to soft foods today—mashed potatoes, scrambled eggs, maybe some oatmeal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-10-28 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have toast? I miss real food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-10-28 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, plain toast is fine. Just go slow—small bites, chew well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-10-28 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And can I restart my multivitamin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-10-28 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we can restart your multivitamin and pantoprazole. But we’ll keep holding the iron for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-10-28 13:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s the soft diet going?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-10-28 13:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good! I ate mashed potatoes and chicken today. Only a little nausea after, but it passed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-10-28 13:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. We’ll keep you on softs tonight and try regular food tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-10-29 07:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. You tolerated soft foods well. We’re going to try a regular diet today—small portions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-10-29 07:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s great! Can I have a sandwich?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-10-29 07:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, turkey or chicken sandwich, no mayo. And keep drinking fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-10-29 07:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my G-tube—do I still need it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-10-29 07:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good question. Since you’re eating better, the bariatric team recommends follow-up to discuss removing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-10-29 07:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’d like that. It’s been a hassle, and I don’t want it if I don’t need it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-10-29 07:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll set that up. For now, keep the site clean. There’s a little crusting, but no signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-10-30 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. You’ve kept down regular meals, no vomiting, and your labs are stable. We’re ready to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-10-30 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great news! What meds should I take at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-10-30 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your usual meds—pantoprazole, gabapentin, fluoxetine, atorvastatin. Restart your iron and multivitamin. And you’ll have Zofran and Compazine for nausea if it comes back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-10-30 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2174-10-30 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See your PCP in a week, and schedule with your bariatric surgeon about the G-tube removal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2174-10-30 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I feel like I’m finally turning a corner."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2174-10-30 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve worked hard for it. Keep resting, eat small meals, and call if nausea or diarrhea returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2174-10-30 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before discharge. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2174-10-30 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. A little tired, but no nausea. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2174-10-30 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Your husband is here, and we’ll have you out within the hour."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2174-10-30 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Here’s your discharge summary. Continue all meds, follow up with your doctors, and focus on nutrition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2174-10-30 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again for taking care of me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2174-10-30 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and feel better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2174-10-30 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m already feeling better. See you at follow-up!"
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-10-26 17:45:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-10-30 13:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was readmitted three days after discharge due to persistent nausea, vomiting, and non-bloody diarrhea that never resolved at home. She had been previously diagnosed with norovirus gastroenteritis and was treated supportively with IV fluids, anti-nausea medications, and gradual advancement of diet from clear liquids to regular meals. Her symptoms improved over four days, and she tolerated oral intake without recurrence of nausea or vomiting. Tube feeds were held during admission to avoid exacerbating diarrhea. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to follow up with her primary care provider and bariatric surgeon regarding G-tube removal.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute gastroenteropathy due to Norwalk agent",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Dehydration",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Unspecified abdominal pain",
      "Hyperlipidemia, unspecified",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Bariatric surgery status"
    ]
  }
}
